@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+# BUG-260823-1vx45a implementation evidence
+
+## Root cause and change
+
+`TestManagerLockHelper` previously registered its subprocess-owned `Operation`
+or `HomeLock` with `testing.T.Cleanup`, then printed `acquired` or `blocked`
+before that cleanup released the Windows file handle. The build-key test also
+left its parent `Operation` to deferred test cleanup. Windows refuses to remove
+the `.lock` file while either handle remains open.
+
+The helper now explicitly closes every acquired lock before publishing a
+result. The build-key test explicitly closes its parent operation. Both named
+tests end with a deterministic lifecycle guard: an opt-in helper releases its
