+# BUG-260823-1vx45a implementation evidence
+
+## Root cause and change
+
+`TestManagerLockHelper` previously registered its subprocess-owned `Operation`
+or `HomeLock` with `testing.T.Cleanup`, then printed `acquired` or `blocked`
+before that cleanup released the Windows file handle. The build-key test also
+left its parent `Operation` to deferred test cleanup. Windows refuses to remove
+the `.lock` file while either handle remains open.
+
+The helper now explicitly closes every acquired lock before publishing a
+result. The build-key test explicitly closes its parent operation. Both named
+tests end with a deterministic lifecycle guard: an opt-in helper releases its
+lock, reports the result, and stays alive while the parent removes the manager
+home. The old deferred-release lifecycle fails this guard on Windows; the new
+lifecycle releases the file without suppressing cleanup errors, moving state
+outside `t.TempDir`, or skipping a test.
+
+## Validation ledger
+
+| Command | Platform | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `go test ./internal/managerlock -run '^(TestSubprocessContentionAndIndependentProjects|TestSubprocessBuildKeyDeduplicationAcrossProjects)$' -count=10` | macOS arm64, Go 1.25.5 | exit 0, `ok`, 8.374s |
+| `go test ./internal/managerlock -count=5` | macOS arm64, Go 1.25.5 | exit 0, `ok`, 6.483s |
+| `go test -race ./internal/managerlock -run '^(TestSubprocessContentionAndIndependentProjects|TestSubprocessBuildKeyDeduplicationAcrossProjects)$' -count=5` | macOS arm64, Go 1.25.5 | exit 0, `ok`, 45.305s |
+| `go test ./internal/managerlock -run '^(TestSubprocessContentionAndIndependentProjects|TestSubprocessBuildKeyDeduplicationAcrossProjects)$' -count=10` | Linux arm64 Lima, Go 1.25.5 | exit 0, `ok`, 6.166s |
+| `go test ./internal/managerlock -count=5` | Linux arm64 Lima, Go 1.25.5 | exit 0, `ok`, 4.393s |
+| `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go test -c ./internal/managerlock -o .temp/BUG-260823-1vx45a/managerlock_windows_amd64.test.exe` | macOS cross-compile | exit 0 |
+| `go vet ./...` | macOS arm64 | exit 0 |
+| `golangci-lint run` | macOS arm64 | exit 0, `0 issues.` |
+| `go build -ldflags '-X github.com/relux-works/curator/internal/version.value=dev' -o .temp/BUG-260823-1vx45a/curator ./cmd/curator` | macOS arm64 | exit 0 |
+| `git diff --check` | macOS arm64 | exit 0 |
+
+The first `go test ./...` attempt found the pinned
+`agents/skills/skill-go-testing-tools` submodule uninitialized and reported the
+`internal/ui` setup failure. After the normal `git submodule update --init
+--recursive agents/skills/skill-go-testing-tools`, the same process continued
+past the repository's 10-minute root-package timeout and left its parent with no
+child process; it was terminated explicitly and returned exit 143. This is
+reported as a failed/inconclusive full-suite gate, not as passing evidence.
+Relevant package, vet, lint, build, macOS, and Linux gates are green.
+
+## Native Windows boundary
+
+The online Tailscale Windows host was reachable but rejected every public key
+already loaded in the local SSH agent for the `administrator` account. Native
+Windows execution was therefore not available in this developer run. The test
+binary compiles for windows/amd64, but the acceptance criterion of five
+consecutive Windows CI runs remains for the commit/PR-owning orchestrator after
+publishing the candidate branch.
+
+Temporary Linux validation installed the checksum-verified official
+`go1.25.5.linux-arm64.tar.gz` under `/tmp/BUG-260823-1vx45a` in the existing
+Lima VM; it did not modify the VM's system toolchain, and the task-scoped
+directory was removed after evidence capture.
